{
  "name": "poly-load-sidecar",
  "status": "experimental",
  "description": "After a pattern file is read and closed, publish the sidecar of the track's ACTIVE pattern letter ('poly<[track+0x2e]>') into the chord bank at CCM 0x1000B530 + track*0x880, whatever letter this load was for. The stock project loader preloads every pattern letter of every track through this same site, and a pattern load for a letter other than the one the player is using used to leave the bank holding another letter's chord (or an empty file's zeros), so playback dropped to mono after a project switch. Restricting the publish to the active letter makes the bank converge on the chord the player will actually use. Missing or short sidecars zero the bank so a previous project's chord cannot leak. Hook 0x0801CD96 (after f_close) -> cave 0x08049000.",
  "cave": {
    "addr": "0x08049000",
    "asm": [
      "mov r12, sp",
      "push {r4-r8, lr}",
